.TH cat "" "Command"
.SH NAME
cat \- concatenate/print files
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcat [\-u] [\fIfile ...\fB]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
cat -- concatenate/print files
Usage:	cat [ -u ] [ file ... ]
Option:	-u	Do not buffer output in 512-byte blocks
File '-' indicates the standard input.
If no 'file' is specified, the standard input is used.
.HE
.B cat
copies each
.I file
in turn to the standard output.
The name
.B \-
means the standard input.
If no
.I file
is given,
.B cat
copies the standard input.
.PP
By default,
.B cat
buffers its output in 512-byte blocks.
.IP \fB\-u\fR
Do not buffer the output; each character is written as soon as it
is read.
This is useful when
.B cat
feeds a pipe or another program that should see the data without
delay.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cp ,
.B pr
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
If a named
.I file
cannot be opened,
.B cat
prints a message naming the file and the reason, skips it, and
continues with the remaining files; the overall exit status is still
zero.
.B cat
exits with status 1 only if a read error occurs on an input file
or a write error occurs on the standard output.
